  "description": "Renders any Markdown (.md) file into a nice-looking, pre-formatted, printable PDF with zero configuration. Markdown is parsed by a vendored C# port of the markdown-it CommonMark parser (with tables, strikethrough, footnotes, task lists, and YAML front matter), converted to HTML with a polished default stylesheet, and rendered through CodeBrix.PdfDocCreate.Html2Pdf. Consumers who want a different look can ask for the generated ready-to-render HTML/CSS instead, restyle it, and hand it to Html2Pdf themselves.",
